course: dictionary
lesson: 3029
title: Eaglet: a small eagle
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An eaglet is a young eagle, a baby or chick. The ending -let means small, so you can often work out a word like this from its ending. Think of piglet, booklet and droplet, which are all small things.
explain: «a Duck and a Dodo, a Lory and an Eaglet» comes from Alice in Wonderland. The other birds in the list help you: a Lory is a small bright parrot, and a Dodo is a big bird that died out long ago. Context clues tell you the Eaglet is a bird too, and a young one.
explain: Eaglets hatch from eggs in a big nest called an eyrie. Both parents feed them until they can fly. When you meet a new word, check its ending and the words around it before you reach for a dictionary.
fact: An eaglet is a young eagle, a baby or chick.
fact: The ending -let means small, as in piglet, booklet and droplet.
fact: In Alice in Wonderland, the Eaglet is a young bird in the pool of tears and the Caucus-race.
fact: «Speak English!» is what the Eaglet tells the Dodo, because it does not understand his long words.
fact: Eaglets hatch from eggs in a big nest called an eyrie, and both parents feed them until they can fly.
exercise: «a Duck and a Dodo, a Lory and an Eaglet» What is an eaglet? | *A young eagle, a baby or chick | A pool of tears | A small bright parrot | A big bird that died out long ago
exercise: Which part of the word eaglet tells you it is small? | The middle, -gl- | *The ending, -let | The start, E- | It is not a clue at all
exercise: «The Eaglet says "Speak English!"» Why does the Eaglet say this? | It has started to rain | The Duck is lost in the pool | The Eaglet wants to sing a song | *The Dodo uses long words the Eaglet does not understand
test: Which word means a young eagle? | *Eaglet | Duck | Lory | Dodo
test: In Alice in Wonderland, who tells the Dodo "Speak English!"? | *The Eaglet | The Lory | The Duck | The Dodo himself
exam: Which ending means small, as in eaglet, piglet and booklet? | -ful | -ish | *-let | -est
